IMPORT prelude

-- Hindu Endowments Act 1968 (Singapore) -- what counts as an endowment (s 2), who may sit on the Board and on a committee of
-- management and how a Board appointment ends (ss 5, 8, 9, 20), the Board's quorum (s 12), when the Minister may hand an endowment
-- to the Board (s 18), the Board's powers over trustees and others and the s 24 offence (ss 22 to 24), the indemnity for acting on
-- the Board's advice (s 25), the bar on suing about an endowment without the Board's order (s 26), sanctioned dealings with
-- endowment land (ss 17, 28), the annual report deadlines (ss 29, 30), personal immunity (s 34A) and political use of temples (s 36).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 1/4/2022), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/HEA1968.txt. The deposit says the revised edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including
-- 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the latest amendment annotated in the body is
-- [Act 25 of 2021 wef 01/04/2022], on s 32(1). The meta file records the version as current at 1 October 2026.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0144 (subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl): Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. The people the Act reaches are trustees and managers of Hindu endowments, anyone holding endowment money, property
-- or documents, would-be litigants about an endowment, and those appointed to the Board or its committees. Not encoded: ss 3, 4
-- (constitution, incorporation), s 6 (Secretary), s 7 (Gazette notice), ss 10, 11 (strangers, chairing, secrecy), ss 13 to 16
-- (seal, officers, minutes, other committees), s 17A (companies), s 19 (vesting and the Registrar of Deeds), s 21 (powers once
-- administered), s 23 (examination) beyond the s 24 offence, s 27 (compromise), ss 31 to 34 (schemes and the High Court), s 35
-- (rules) and s 37 (transfer from the Muslim and Hindu Endowments Board in 1969). No rules under s 35 were retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions as shown in the example rows. No
-- pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Hindu Endowments Act 1968 -- endowments`

GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER, `y` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS
    IF `x` AT LEAST `y` THEN `x` ELSE `y`

§§ `2 -- what an endowment is`

-- s 2: "endowment" means "any endowment in land, building or money given or to be given for the support of any Hindu temple or
-- Hindu shrine or school or other Hindu pious, religious, charitable or beneficial purpose".
-- The definition names land, building and money only. Whether "school" must itself be Hindu is not spelt out; the words "other
-- Hindu ... purpose" suggest it (an inference), and a Hindu school is the only school case encoded.
DECLARE Gift IS ONE OF
    `land`
    `a building`
    `money`
    `other movable property`

DECLARE Purpose IS ONE OF
    `a Hindu temple`
    `a Hindu shrine`
    `a Hindu school`
    `another Hindu pious, religious, charitable or beneficial purpose`
    `a non-Hindu religious purpose`
    `a private family purpose`

GIVEN `the gift` IS A Gift, `the purpose` IS A Purpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is an endowment under s 2` IF
        (NOT (`the gift` EQUALS `other movable property`))
    AND (NOT (`the purpose` EQUALS `a non-Hindu religious purpose`))
    AND (NOT (`the purpose` EQUALS `a private family purpose`))

§§ `5, 20 -- who may be appointed`

-- s 5(1): the Board is a Chairman, a Vice-Chairman, a Finance member and "not less than 8 and not more than 12 other members, all
-- of whom shall be appointed by the Minister". (2) appointments are for 3 years unless the instrument says otherwise.
-- s 5(4) and s 20(5): no person shall be appointed a member of the Board, or of a committee of management, "unless he -- (a) is a
-- Hindu; and (b) is a citizen of Singapore".
GIVEN `is a Hindu` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a citizen of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may be appointed to the Board or a committee of management` IF
    `is a Hindu` AND `is a citizen of Singapore`

GIVEN `other members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the number of other members complies with s 5(1)(d)` IF
    `other members` AT LEAST 8 AND `other members` AT MOST 12

-- s 5(3): members are eligible for re-appointment "except that a Finance member shall not be appointed for more than 2 consecutive
-- terms as a Finance member but may, at the end of the second consecutive term, be appointed in any capacity in the Board except as
-- a Finance member".
DECLARE Capacity IS ONE OF
    `Chairman`
    `Vice-Chairman`
    `Finance member`
    `other member`

GIVEN `the capacity` IS A Capacity, `consecutive terms just served as Finance member` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the re-appointment is permitted by s 5(3)` IF
        (NOT (`the capacity` EQUALS `Finance member`))
    OR  `consecutive terms just served as Finance member` LESS THAN 2

-- s 20(2): a committee of management consists "of at least one member of the Board, and of not more than 11 other persons".
-- (3) it meets at least once a month and "the quorum at all meetings of the committee shall be 6 members present".
-- (4) members are appointed "for a period of not more than 3 years" and are eligible for re-appointment.
GIVEN `Board members on the committee` IS A NUMBER, `other persons on the committee` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the committee of management is constituted as s 20(2) requires` IF
    `Board members on the committee` AT LEAST 1 AND `other persons on the committee` AT MOST 11

GIVEN `committee members present` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the committee meeting is quorate under s 20(3)` IF
    `committee members present` AT LEAST 6

GIVEN `years of the committee appointment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the committee appointment period is within s 20(4)` IF
    `years of the committee appointment` AT MOST 3

§§ `8, 9 -- how a Board appointment ends`

-- s 8: the appointment of any member "determines -- (a) upon his death; (b) if he resigns his appointment, by writing addressed to
-- the Minister through the Secretary of the Board; (c) if he is absent from Singapore, without written permission from the
-- Chairman, for a period exceeding 3 months; or (d) if he is declared a bankrupt".
GIVEN `has died` IS A BOOLEAN, `resigned in writing to the Minister through the Secretary` IS A BOOLEAN, `months absent from Singapore` IS A NUMBER, `had the Chairman's written permission` IS A BOOLEAN, `declared a bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appointment determines under s 8` IF
        `has died`
    OR  `resigned in writing to the Minister through the Secretary`
    OR  ((NOT `had the Chairman's written permission`) AND `months absent from Singapore` GREATER THAN 3)
    OR  `declared a bankrupt`

-- s 9: the Minister may revoke an appointment "(a) if the conduct of the member ... is in the opinion of the Minister such as to
-- bring discredit upon the Board; (b) if for any reason the member becomes unable properly to carry out the duties ...; (c) if,
-- without due cause to be approved by the Chairman, the member absents himself from 3 successive meetings of the Board; or (d) if
-- the Minister considers it desirable in the public interest".
GIVEN `conduct brings discredit in the Minister's opinion` IS A BOOLEAN, `unable to carry out the duties` IS A BOOLEAN, `successive meetings missed` IS A NUMBER, `cause approved by the Chairman` IS A BOOLEAN, `public interest in the Minister's view` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may revoke the appointment under s 9` IF
        `conduct brings discredit in the Minister's opinion`
    OR  `unable to carry out the duties`
    OR  ((NOT `cause approved by the Chairman`) AND `successive meetings missed` AT LEAST 3)
    OR  `public interest in the Minister's view`

§§ `12 -- quorum of the Board`

-- s 12(1): "No business, except that of adjournment, shall be transacted and no action or resolution of the Board shall be valid
-- unless at least 7 members or one-third of the members, whichever is the greater, are present at the meeting."
-- (2) the Board may act notwithstanding a vacancy. "the members" is read as the members in office (an inference).
-- Under s 5(1) the Board has 11 to 15 members, so one-third is at most 5 and the 7-member floor always governs.
GIVEN `members in office` IS A NUMBER, `members present` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board meeting is quorate under s 12` IF
    `members present` AT LEAST `the greater of` 7 (`members in office` DIVIDED BY 3)

GIVEN `members in office` IS A NUMBER, `members present` IS A NUMBER, `the business is adjournment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may transact the business` IF
    `the business is adjournment` OR `the Board meeting is quorate under s 12` `members in office` `members present`

§§ `18 -- when the Minister may order the Board to administer an endowment`

-- s 18(1): "Whenever it appears to the Minister on the report of the Board that -- (a) any endowment has been mismanaged; (b) there
-- are no trustees appointed for the management of any endowment; or (c) it would be otherwise to the advantage of any endowment that
-- it should be administered by the Board, the Minister may order that the endowment shall be administered by the Board."
-- (2): "The persons who manage the endowment shall be given an opportunity to make representations to the Minister within such
-- period as the Minister may specify before an order is made".
-- s 19(1): from the order, all the property, movable and immovable, vests in the Board on the endowment's trusts.
GIVEN `the Board has reported` IS A BOOLEAN, `mismanaged` IS A BOOLEAN, `no trustees appointed` IS A BOOLEAN, `otherwise to the endowment's advantage` IS A BOOLEAN, `managers were given an opportunity to make representations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may order the Board to administer the endowment` IF
        `the Board has reported`
    AND (`mismanaged` OR `no trustees appointed` OR `otherwise to the endowment's advantage`)
    AND `managers were given an opportunity to make representations`

§§ `22 to 24 -- accounts, examination and the offence`

-- s 22(1): the Board "may at any time require written accounts and statements and answers to enquiries" from "(a) trustees or
-- persons who are or have been at any time acting or concerned in the administration of the endowment ...; (b) agents of any such
-- trustees or persons; (c) persons having possession, custody or control of any funds or moneys of the endowment; (d) persons in the
-- beneficial receipt of any funds thereof or of any income or stipend therefrom; (e) persons in the possession or occupation or
-- management of any property thereof; (f) persons having the possession, custody or control of any documents". (2) verified on oath
-- or affirmation.
DECLARE Person IS ONE OF
    `a current trustee`
    `a former trustee`
    `an agent of a trustee`
    `a person holding the endowment's funds`
    `a priest receiving a stipend from the endowment`
    `a tenant of endowment property`
    `a person holding the endowment's documents`
    `a worshipper with no other connection`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may require accounts from the person under s 22` IF
    NOT (`the person` EQUALS `a worshipper with no other connection`)

-- s 24: "Any person who refuses or wilfully neglects to comply with any requisition or order of the Board made under this Act, or
-- destroys or withholds any document required to be produced or transmitted by him, shall be guilty of an offence and shall be
-- liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $5,000 and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding $50
-- for every day during which the offence continues after conviction." [12/2010] No imprisonment is provided.
GIVEN `a requisition or order was made under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `refused` IS A BOOLEAN, `wilfully neglected` IS A BOOLEAN, `destroyed or withheld a required document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is an offence under s 24` IF
    `a requisition or order was made under the Act` AND (`refused` OR `wilfully neglected` OR `destroyed or withheld a required document`)

GIVEN `days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum s 24 fine` MEANS
    5000 PLUS 50 TIMES `days continuing after conviction`

§§ `25 -- acting on the Board's advice`

-- s 25(1): the Board "shall consider all applications" by a trustee or other person concerned in managing an endowment for its
-- opinion or advice, and "may" give it. (2): the advice "shall be in writing under the seal of the Board, and every trustee and
-- other person who acts upon or in accordance with the opinion or advice ... shall ... be deemed and taken so far as respects his own
-- responsibility to have acted in accordance with his trust". (3): no later High Court order impairs that indemnity. (4): nothing
-- indemnifies a person "guilty of any fraud or of any wilful concealment or misrepresentation in obtaining the opinion or advice".
GIVEN `the advice was in writing under seal` IS A BOOLEAN, `acted in accordance with the advice` IS A BOOLEAN, `fraud, concealment or misrepresentation in obtaining it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is deemed to have acted in accordance with the trust` IF
        `the advice was in writing under seal`
    AND `acted in accordance with the advice`
    AND (NOT `fraud, concealment or misrepresentation in obtaining it`)

§§ `26 -- suing about an endowment`

-- s 26(1): "Before any legal proceeding for obtaining any relief, order or direction concerning or relating to any endowment ... is
-- commenced or taken by any person, the person shall transmit to the Board notice in writing of the proposed proceeding".
-- (4): "no legal proceeding for obtaining any such relief, order or direction shall be entertained or proceeded with by the General
-- Division of the High Court or by any court or judge except upon and in conformity with an order of the Board".
-- (5): "Nothing in this Act shall extend to or affect any legal proceeding in which any person claims any property or seeks any
-- relief adversely to any endowment."
-- The text says "any endowment"; it does not confine s 26 to endowments the Board administers under s 18.
GIVEN `the proceeding relates to an endowment` IS A BOOLEAN, `the claim is adverse to the endowment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `notice to the Board must come first under s 26(1)` IF
    `the proceeding relates to an endowment` AND (NOT `the claim is adverse to the endowment`)

GIVEN `the proceeding relates to an endowment` IS A BOOLEAN, `the claim is adverse to the endowment` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Board has ordered it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a court may entertain the proceeding under s 26` IF
        (NOT `notice to the Board must come first under s 26(1)` `the proceeding relates to an endowment` `the claim is adverse to the endowment`)
    OR  `the Board has ordered it`

§§ `17, 28 -- dealing with endowment land`

-- s 28: whenever "any endowment administered by it would be benefited by -- (a) letting any part of the lands or buildings thereof,
-- other than any temple or the grounds thereof, on occupation or lease; (b) digging for or raising stone, clay, sand, gravel or other
-- minerals; (c) cutting timber ...; (d) forming any new road or street; (e) ... drains or sewers; (f) erecting new buildings or
-- fences; (g) the repair, alteration, extension, rebuilding or removal of any existing building; (h) making any improvements ...; or
-- (i) the sale or exchange of any lands or buildings, other than any temple or the grounds thereof", the Board may do it "although
-- such leases or acts are not specifically authorised or permitted by the trusts of the endowment".
DECLARE Dealing IS ONE OF
    `letting land or buildings`
    `digging for stone, clay, sand or gravel`
    `cutting timber`
    `forming a new road`
    `erecting new buildings or fences`
    `rebuilding or removing an existing building`
    `selling or exchanging land or buildings`

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing, `administered by the Board` IS A BOOLEAN, `the endowment would benefit` IS A BOOLEAN, `it concerns a temple or its grounds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may sanction it under s 28` IF
        `administered by the Board`
    AND `the endowment would benefit`
    AND (NOT ((`the dealing` EQUALS `letting land or buildings` OR `the dealing` EQUALS `selling or exchanging land or buildings`)
              AND `it concerns a temple or its grounds`))

-- s 17(1)(c): the Board may "convey, assign, ... mortgage, demise, ... lease, ... transfer or otherwise dispose of, or deal with, any
-- movable or immovable property vested in, belonging to or acquired by the Board upon such terms as the Board thinks fit".
-- (2): it may do so "notwithstanding section 19 or a trust or condition (express or implied) prohibiting or restricting" it.
-- s 17 has no temple exception. How it sits with the temple exception in s 28 the text does not say; this rule encodes s 17 alone.
GIVEN `the property is vested in the Board` IS A BOOLEAN, `a trust prohibits the disposal` IS A BOOLEAN, `the property is a temple` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may dispose of the property under s 17` IF
    `the property is vested in the Board`

§§ `29, 30 -- the annual report`

-- s 29(1): the Secretary shall, "as soon as possible after 31 March of every year but not later than 31 December of that year",
-- submit to a meeting of the Board a report for the preceding financial year with a balance sheet as at 31 March, an income and
-- expenditure account and a list of properties and investments of each endowment. (2) audited first by an auditor appointed by the
-- Board and approved by the Minister. (3) "financial year" means 12 months ending on 31 March.
-- s 30: "within 14 days after the meeting" the Secretary shall submit the report and accounts to the Minister and cause them to be
-- published in the Gazette and "exhibited in all temples administered by the Board".
-- Dates are written as YYYYMMDD numbers.
GIVEN `year in which the financial year ended` IS A NUMBER, `date submitted to the Board meeting` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the annual report is within the s 29(1) window` IF
        `date submitted to the Board meeting` GREATER THAN `year in which the financial year ended` TIMES 10000 PLUS 331
    AND `date submitted to the Board meeting` AT MOST `year in which the financial year ended` TIMES 10000 PLUS 1231

GIVEN `days after the meeting` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the report is published and exhibited in time under s 30` IF
    `days after the meeting` AT MOST 14

§§ `34A -- personal immunity`

-- s 34A: "No suit or other legal proceedings shall lie personally against -- (a) any member of the Board; (b) the Secretary of the
-- Board; or (c) any employee of the Board or other person acting under the direction of the Board, for anything which is in good
-- faith done or intended to be done by him in the execution or purported execution of this Act."
DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    `a Board member`
    `the Secretary`
    `a Board employee`
    `a person acting under the Board's direction`
    `a private trustee acting on his own`

GIVEN `the actor` IS AN Actor, `in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `in execution or purported execution of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a personal suit is barred by s 34A` IF
        (NOT (`the actor` EQUALS `a private trustee acting on his own`))
    AND `in good faith`
    AND `in execution or purported execution of the Act`

§§ `36 -- no political use of temples`

-- s 36: "The Board or any committee of management shall not permit the temples administered by the Board or any part of any land or
-- premises belonging to any endowment to be used for political purposes." The duty is on the Board and committees; the Act attaches
-- no penalty to it and does not define "political purposes".
GIVEN `a temple administered by the Board` IS A BOOLEAN, `land or premises of an endowment` IS A BOOLEAN, `the use is political` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board or committee must not permit the use under s 36` IF
    (`a temple administered by the Board` OR `land or premises of an endowment`) AND `the use is political`
